{
  "sn22.99:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.99 ",
  "sn22.99:0.2": "10. Flowers ",
  "sn22.99:0.3": "A Leash ",
  "sn22.99:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn22.99:1.2": "“Mendicants, this transmigration has no known beginning. ",
  "sn22.99:1.3": "No first point is found of sentient beings roaming and transmigrating, shrouded by ignorance and fettered by craving. ",
  "sn22.99:1.4": "There comes a time when the ocean dries up and evaporates and is no more. ",
  "sn22.99:1.5": "But in any case, there is no making an end of suffering for sentient beings roaming and transmigrating, shrouded by ignorance and fettered by craving, I say. ",
  "sn22.99:1.6": "There comes a time when Sineru the king of mountains is burned up and destroyed, and is no more. ",
  "sn22.99:1.7": "But in any case, there is no making an end of suffering for sentient beings roaming and transmigrating, shrouded by ignorance and fettered by craving, I say. ",
  "sn22.99:1.8": "There comes a time when the great earth is burned up and destroyed, and is no more. ",
  "sn22.99:1.9": "But in any case, there is no making an end of suffering for sentient beings roaming and transmigrating, shrouded by ignorance and fettered by craving, I say. ",
  "sn22.99:2.1": "Suppose a hound on a leash was tethered to a strong post or pillar. It would just keep running and circling around that post or pillar. ",
  "sn22.99:2.2": "In the same way, take an unlearned ordinary person who has not seen the noble ones, and is neither skilled nor trained in their teaching. They